pageType: content
notes: |
  Falsification criteria slide. Outlines four rigorous, observable conditions that would falsify the commercial fusion thesis: failure to demonstrate TBR >= 1.05 in hardware; first-wall replacement intervals under 6 months; irreversible HTS neutron degradation; and economic preemption by advanced fission SMRs or deep geothermal below $45/MWh. Establishes milestone-gated risk management for institutional investors.
elements:
  # Header Kicker
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 26, 600, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      text: "09 · FALSIFICATION CRITERIA"

  # Header Title
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 42, 860, 30]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      text: "Four Observable Hard Thresholds Would Falsify the Commercial Fusion Investment Thesis"

  # Header Subtitle
  - elementId: subtitle
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 72, 860, 16]
    content:
      style: "$subtitle"
      text: "Boundary conditions where technological or economic failure invalidates the commercial investment case"

  # Header Divider
  - elementId: header-line
    elementType: line
    bounds: [50, 92, 860, 1]
    points: "0,0 860,0"
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  # Pillar 1 - Card
  - elementId: col-1-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 203, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-1-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 203, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 111, 187, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "1. TRITIUM DEFICIT"

  - elementId: col-1-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 142, 187, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.2
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Observable Test:</b></p>
        <p>Integrated blanket test modules fail to demonstrate net breeding (\( \mathrm{TBR} &lt; 1.02 \)) due to structural parasitic neutron capture or extraction chemistry losses.</p>
        <p><br><b>Fatal Impact:</b></p>
        <p>DT fusion encounters a hard physical fuel ceiling by 2038 as global CANDU civilian reserves exhaust. Industry is permanently capped at &lt;3 prototype plants without fuel.</p>

  # Pillar 2 - Card
  - elementId: col-2-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [269, 106, 203, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-2-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [269, 106, 203, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [277, 111, 187, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "2. NEUTRON DAMAGE"

  - elementId: col-2-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [277, 142, 187, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.2
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Observable Test:</b></p>
        <p>14.1 MeV neutron helium embrittlement causes premature fracture or void swelling in first-wall steels, forcing core vessel replacements every <b>&lt;6 months</b>.</p>
        <p><br><b>Fatal Impact:</b></p>
        <p>Plant availability collapses below 50%; recurring replacement capital expenses and radioactive waste handling push LCOE &gt;$180/MWh, eliminating economic viability.</p>

  # Pillar 3 - Card
  - elementId: col-3-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [488, 106, 203, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-3-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [488, 106, 203, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [496, 111, 187, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "3. HTS DEGRADATION"

  - elementId: col-3-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [496, 142, 187, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.2
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Observable Test:</b></p>
        <p>Fast neutron flux degrades REBCO critical current \( J_c \) by &gt;15% per operating year, and room-temperature thermal annealing fails to restore superconductor pinning.</p>
        <p><br><b>Fatal Impact:</b></p>
        <p>The 20-year magnet capital amortization model breaks; replacing high-field toroidal coil sets every 3 years renders the capital expenditure un-bankable.</p>

  # Pillar 4 - Card
  - elementId: col-4-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [707, 106, 203, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-4-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [707, 106, 203, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: col-4-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [715, 111, 187, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "4. BASELOAD PREEMPTION"

  - elementId: col-4-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [715, 142, 187, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.2
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Observable Test:</b></p>
        <p>Advanced Gen-IV fission SMRs, deep enhanced geothermal (EGS), or multi-day storage achieve commercial scale at <b>&lt;$45/MWh firm power</b> before 2035.</p>
        <p><br><b>Fatal Impact:</b></p>
        <p>The commercial market window for fusion closes before NOAK scale is reached; fusion is relegated to niche applications (space propulsion, naval combatants).</p>

  # Watch Indicators Band
  - elementId: watch-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 384, 860, 74]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$tagRed"}

  - elementId: watch-accent
